================================================================================
Word frequencies — overview
================================================================================
CleverKeys' word lists come from three CC BY-SA sources, selected per list:

  List                                              Source
  ------------------------------------------------  -----------------------------
  bundled dictionaries (src/main/assets/            wordfreq (+ AOSP LatinIME
    dictionaries/) and langpack-<lang>.zip for        inclusion oracle where noted
    en, es, fr, de, it, nl, pt, sv, ru, el, tr, he,   below)
    uk, bg, mk, id, ms, tl; langpack-en-wordfreq.zip
  langpack-en-opensubtitles.zip,                    FrequencyWords (OpenSubtitles)
    langpack-en-opensubtitles-50k.zip
  langpack-sw.zip                                   Swwiki (Swahili Wikipedia)

Every list is modified: words were selected, filtered and ranked, and their
frequencies quantised into CleverKeys' binary dictionary format ("converted to
a CleverKeys frequency list"). Each langpack-*.zip carries its own NOTICE.txt
and "license" / "attribution" / "source" manifest keys, so the attribution
travels with a pack downloaded on its own (scripts/build_langpack.py;
docs/audit/2026-09-26-data-licensing-audit.md).

CC BY-SA 4.0 adaptations may be licensed under GPLv3
(https://creativecommons.org/compatible-licenses/; conditions at
https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/ShareAlike_compatibility:_GPLv3 — keep
the attribution, licence notice and link, indicate changes). CleverKeys
distributes these adapted lists under GPL-3.0-only, with the attribution below.

